    {
      "node_id": "kg_doc_5",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Mehtab Abbasi (Urdu/Pashto/Hindko: سردار مهتاب احمد خان عباسي ) is a Pakistani politician from Abbottabad who started his political career as an independent candidate in the 1985 election, and after this election subsequently took hold of both the provincial and national assembly seat in his constituency winning repeatedly and without loss until the 2013 election. Sardar Mehtab also served as Governor of Khyber Pakhtunkhwa, Pakistan from 2014 to 2016, Chief Minister of Khyber Pakhtunkhwa from 1997 to 1999, and Federal Minister for Railways in 2008. He is politically affiliated with Pakistan Muslim League (N). He has served as a senator for five years since March 2003, until he won the NA-17 Abbottabad-I seat for the National Assembly of Pakistan in the 2008 general election.",
      "depth": 0,
